<?xml version='1.0' ?>
<rrx namespace="Intellocate" v="9.1.6">
  <com ref="Datacap.Libraries.Intellocate.Actions"  qi=": Actions that manipulates zones and assign page types">
    <h>
      <b>Intellocate action library</b>

      <b>Details:</b>
      The Intellocate action library actions focus on positions of fields and line items in a page's runtime DCO xml file.
      This is in support of "Intellocate" functionality where zones positions can be assigned at runtime
      to setup new page formats.<br/><br/>

      The fields zoned positions are written in App.xml file e.g. APT.XML file.
      The new position will saved in XML with POS and template Id, e.g. POS 556.
      The Line Item zoned position are also written to APP.xml file which
      is present in the application location App\DCO_App\App.xml, the application's
      setup DCO. e.g. Datacap\APT\dco_APT\APT.xml.<br/><br/>

      <b>Usage:</b> It will write Position corresponding of a new fingerprint's zoned fields and line items from a page's data file(xml)
      to Pos properties of the corresponding Field object and line item objects in the Document hierarchy file(App.xml).<br/><br/>

      <b>Smart parameters:</b> AssignPageType supports smart parameters. Rather than passing connection string hard-coded,
      you can pass as a smart parameter, e.g.  @APPVAR(*/fingerprintconn:cs), it will read values from Application
      .App file which is configured using the Application Service.
      Smart parameters are special identifiers that are evaluated at runtime allowing action input parameters
      to change based on the current state of the batch or environment.<br/><br/>

    </h>

    <method name="SetZones">
      <ap>None.</ap>
      <h>
        Writes the position coordinates of a new fingerprint's zoned fields from a page's Data
        file to the Pos properties of the corresponding Field objects in the Document Hierarchy file (.xml).
        <e>
          <b>SetZones()</b><br/>
          This will set zones of the fields in App.xml file, also known as the setup DCO.
        </e>
      </h>
      <lvl>Page level only.</lvl>
      <ret>
        <b>False</b> if a fingerprint match has not occurred, or if the Document Hierarchy file
        (.xml) cannot be saved.  Otherwise, <b>True.</b>
      </ret>
      <see>
        Refer to the top-level help for more information about this action library.
      </see>
    </method>

    <method name ="SetDetailZone">
      <ap>None.</ap>
      <h>
        Writes the position coordinates of a new fingerprint's Detail Line fields
        from a page's Data file to the Pos properties of the corresponding Detail Line
        Field objects of the application's Document Hierarchy.
        <e>
          <b>SetDetailZone()</b><br/>
          It will write Detail Position coordinates to App.xml file.
        </e>
      </h>
      <lvl>Page level only.</lvl>
      <ret>
        Always <b>True.</b>
      </ret>
      <see>
        Refer to the top-level help for more information about this action library.
      </see>
    </method>


    <method name="AdjustZones">
      <ap>None.</ap>
      <h>
        Updates the zoned field position on each respective fingerprint stored in database,
        for all the fields of the page in App.XML file present
        under APP_DCO folder.<br/>
        In the format: <b> Pos templateId Position </b><br/>

        Updates fingerprint-specific position coordinates for Field objects in the
        Document Hierarchy based on the locations listed for the current source page's Data file (.xml)<br/><br/>
        This action is designed to be used on existing fingerprints only.  It will only update fields
        that do not have position information.  Existing fields will not be updated, even if the position
        information for those fields has changed.<br/><br/>
        <e>
          <b>AdjustZones()</b><br/>
          It will update the zones position of all the fields in the page in the APP.XML file as per the respective fingerprint coordinates.<br/>
          e.g. Pos 1074(fingerprint) "Position".<br/><br/>
        </e>
      </h>
      <lvl>Page level only.</lvl>
      <ret>
        <b>False</b> if a fingerprint match has not occurred and a Template ID
        value has not been assigned to the current page, or if the Document
        Hierarchy file cannot be saved. Otherwise, <b>True.</b>
      </ret>
    </method>

    <method name="IsPageDataMissing">
      <ap>None.</ap>
      <h>
        Checks to see that the current page data exists.
        This action does not physically check for the existence of a data file.  It confirms
        that a valid page data is loaded into memory.<br/>
        It verifies whether the current page contains children field objects.<br/>
        If it has no children it will return true. i.e. Page Data is missing, otherwise it will return false.<br/><br/>
        <e>
          <b>IsPageDataMissing()</b><br/>
          This action will check whether there are any children on the current page.
          If the page doesn't have any children then it will return true.
          If the page does contain children it will return false and continue with the next function
          in the rule.<br/><br/>
        </e>
      </h>
      <lvl>Page level only.</lvl>
      <ret>
        <b>True</b> if the current page does not have page data. Otherwise, <b>False.</b>
      </ret>
      <see>
        Refer to the top-level help for more information about this action library.
      </see>
    </method>

    <method name="AssignPageType" >
      <p name="PageType"/>
      <p name ="ConnectionString"/>
      <ap>
        <b>PageType:</b> The value of the page type to assign to the current page.
        PageType is stored in table in fingerprint Database.
        It can be numeric value, which will be stored against particular pagetype.<br/>
        It can also be a alpha-numeric value, which will be stored in table and a numeric id will be automatically generated.<br/><br/>

        <b>ConnectionString:</b>The ConnectionString should be passed so that Connection to fingerprint happens
        and it will write the new pagetype and update template in fingerprint database<br/><br/>

        Smart parameters are supported for all parameters.<br/><br/>

      </ap>
      <h>
        Assigns a required Page Type value to a newly created fingerprint.
        The assigned value corresponds to the values configured in the PageType table within the fingerprint database.
        These values are custom defined for each application.
        If the page type is non-numeric, this action will look up the corresponding numeric value within the database.<br/>
        <e>
          <b>AssignPageType("2", @APPVAR(*/fingerprintconn:cs))</b><br/>
          This example assigns a page type of 2 to the new fingerprint.<br/>
          It will read the fingerprint database connection string configured in the
          Application Manager.<br/><br/>

          <b>AssignPageType("PageSeparator", @APPVAR(*/fingerprintconn:cs))</b><br/>
          This example assigns a page type of "PageSeparator" to the new fingerprint.<br/>
          It will read the fingerprint database connection string configured in the
          Application Manager.<br/><br/>
        </e>
      </h>
      <lvl>Page level only.</lvl>
      <ret>
        <b>False</b> if the numeric value cannot be retrieved from the fingerprint database or if there is
        no connection to the fingerprint database. Otherwise, <b>True.</b>
      </ret>
      <see>
        Refer to the top-level help for more information about this action library.
      </see>
    </method>

  </com>
</rrx>